      "title": "I understood gender discrimination once I added “Mr.” to my resume",
      "author": "Lisa2000",
      "time_utc": "2013-07-12T16:42:42Z",
      "url": "http://qz.com/103453/i-understood-gender-discrimination-after-i-added-mr-to-my-resume-and-landed-a-job/",
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=6033567",
      "score": 643,
      "comments": 376,
      "archive_score": 643,
      "archive_comments": 376,
      "score_source": "algolia",
      "comments_source": "algolia",
      "checked_at": "2026-11-18T10:38:34Z",
      "current_dead": null,
      "current_deleted": null,
      "current_title": "I understood gender discrimination once I added “Mr.” to my resume",
      "excerpt": "\"I made one change that day. I put Mr. in front of my name [Kim] on my CV. It looked a little too formal for my liking but I got an interview for the very next job I applied for. And the one after that. It all happened in a fortnight, and the second job was a substantial increase in responsibility over anything I had done before. In the end I beat out a very competitive short-list and enjoyed that job for the next few years, further enhancing my career.\"",
      "rank": 16,
      "guide_zh": "求职者在简历姓名前加上“先生”后接连获得面试，由此反思性别歧视。"
    },
